      "id": "valid-navigation",
      "title": "Only valid steps can move on",
      "interviewerPrompt": "Build the three steps first. A step can only move on when its data is valid, and going back must never lose what the user typed.",
      "constraints": [
        "Keep the Next button enabled. A disabled button cannot tell the user what is missing.",
        "Pressing Next on an invalid step stays on that step and shows each problem in an element with the class `error` inside that field. A new step starts with no errors.",
        "Name, Street, City and Country cannot be empty or only spaces. Email needs a basic valid format such as `jane@example.com`. Postal code is optional.",
        "Fixing a field removes its error right away.",
        "Back keeps everything the user typed. Keep the starter classes `subtitle`, `step-title`, `field`, `actions` and `summary`, and the order of the fields and buttons."
      ],
